# Chromium profiles created by tooling (harness scenes, store-screenshot capture): browsing history,
# cookies and caches of whatever was open. Matches at any depth — `harness/.profile-lab/`,
# `docs/store/.profile-shots/`, … None of it may ever be committed.
.profile-*/

# harness: everything under harness/out/ is machine-local — Chromium profiles, per-scene evidence dirs
# (screenshots, downloads, panel dumps), fake-Drive trees, brain logs, pid files, executed notebooks, and every
# `--real` result (which carries real portal content and local paths). The ONLY exceptions are the six fake-scene
# verdicts below: synthetic data start to finish, and the evidence README + docs/JUDGES.md point at. Keep this an
# allow-list — a new `harness/out/*` file must be named here on purpose before it can ship.
harness/.profile-*/
harness/out/*
!harness/out/vault-sync.json
!harness/out/lab.json
!harness/out/team-ops.json
!harness/out/courseware.json
!harness/out/scaffold.json
!harness/out/pitch-deck.json
harness/fake-wsp/__pycache__/
